# Semantic theme tokens are required

- All UI must work in both light and dark themes.
- Use the semantic utilities defined in `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`: `background`, `foreground`, `surface`, `elevated`, `border`, `brand`, `muted`, `secondary`, `success`, `warning`, `error`, `info`, and `agent`.
- Do not use fixed Tailwind palette utilities such as `bg-zinc-900`, `text-amber-400`, `border-slate-700`, or `text-red-400` in product UI.
- Prefer `bg-surface`, `bg-elevated`, `text-foreground`, `text-secondary`, `text-muted`, `border-border`, `text-brand`, `text-warning`, and `text-error`.
- Opacity variants of semantic tokens are allowed, for example `bg-brand/10` and `border-warning/30`.
- Do not use `prose-invert` unconditionally; typography must inherit the active theme.
- When fixing a theme regression, add a test that prevents fixed palette utilities from returning in the affected component.
